{
  "dom_id": "step-e14728",
  "name": "Example: Calculating an Unknown Quantity Given a Description of a Triangle",
  "problem": "Consider a triangle $\\triangle ABC$, where $m\\angle{A} = 55^\\circ$, $m\\angle B = x + 10^\\circ$, and $m\\angle C = 3x - 5^\\circ.$ Find the value of $x.$",
  "worked_solution": "The sum of the measures of the interior angles must be $180^\\circ.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{55}^{∘}+(x+{10}^{∘})+(3x-{5}^{∘}) & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {60}^{∘}+4x & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 4x & ={120}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
